 "text": "The men broke the frozen earth with pickaxes, digging foxholes and connecting trenches. They strung barbed wire, and laid trip flares in front of their positions that would light up at a touch. Trenches linked the positions, so ammunition and wounded could move between them out of the enemy's line of fire.",
